Requirements: 23   with obligations: 22   deliberately none: 1

[task-01] Requirement decomposition must preserve two distinctions when it reads a task
    file.
    -> preserve-two-task-distinctions  [invariant/explicit]
       Preserve the two distinctions that matter when reading a task file: acceptance
       criteria versus the behavior they describe, and scope exclusions versus work the
       change must do.
    -> acceptance-criteria-vs-behavior-distinction  [functional/explicit]
       Preserve the distinction between an acceptance criterion that demands a test and
       the behavior that test is about.
    -> scope-exclusion-vs-work-distinction  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves task-03)
       Preserve the distinction between a scope exclusion bullet and work the change
       must do.

[task-02] An acceptance criterion that demands a test states a different requirement
    from the behaviour that test is about. Code that already exhibits the behaviour,
    with nobody having written the test, satisfies one of those requirements and
    violates the other.
    -> test-demand-is-distinct-from-behavior  [functional/explicit]
       Treat an acceptance criterion that demands a test as a different requirement from
       the behavior that test is about.
    -> behavior-alone-does-not-satisfy-test-demand  [regression/explicit]
       Recognize that existing behavior without the test satisfies the behavior
       requirement but not the test-demanding requirement.

[task-03] A bullet under a scope exclusions heading names work the change must not do.
    It never names work the change must do.
    -> scope-exclusion-vs-work-distinction  [invariant/explicit]   (also serves task-01)
       Preserve the distinction between a scope exclusion bullet and work the change
       must do.
    -> scope-exclusion-never-names-required-work  [invariant/explicit]
       Preserve the property that a scope-exclusion bullet does not name work the change
       must do.

[constraint-01] An acceptance criterion that demands a test yields an obligation whose
    demand is the test, not the behaviour the test is about.
    -> test-demand-not-behaviour  [functional/explicit]
       An acceptance criterion that demands a test yields an obligation whose demand is
       the test, not the behaviour the test is about.

[constraint-02] An obligation demanding a behaviour and an obligation demanding a test
    of that behaviour are never recognised as stating the same requirement.
    -> behaviour-and-test-not-same-requirement  [invariant/explicit]
       An obligation demanding a behaviour and an obligation demanding a test of that
       behaviour are never recognised as stating the same requirement.

[constraint-03] A sentence of a given shape yields the same kind of obligation
    regardless of which task file it appears in.
    -> same-shape-same-obligation-kind  [invariant/explicit]
       A sentence with the specified shape yields the same kind of obligation in every
       task file.

[constraint-04] Sibling bullets under one scope exclusions heading receive the same
    disposition as each other.
    -> sibling-scope-exclusions-same-disposition-2  [invariant/explicit]
       Sibling bullets under one scope exclusions heading receive matching dispositions.

[constraint-05] A requirement disposed of without an obligation carries a reason that
    does not itself state a property the change must preserve.
    -> no-preservation-property-in-no-obligation-reason  [invariant/explicit]
       A no-obligation disposition includes a reason that does not itself state a
       property the change must preserve.

[constraint-06] No obligation is produced whose only satisfying evidence would be a test
    that an excluded thing did not happen.
    -> no-obligation-for-excluded-thing-not-happened-test-only  [error_handling/explicit]
       No obligation is produced whose only satisfying evidence would be a test that an
       excluded thing did not happen.

[constraint-07] Two runs over byte-identical task text produce byte-identical review
    state.
    -> byte-identical-task-text-byte-identical-review-state  [regression/explicit]   (also serves completion-06)
       Two runs over byte-identical task text produce byte-identical review state.

[constraint-08] Tests issue no live model calls.
    -> tests-issue-no-live-model-calls  [compatibility/explicit]
       Tests issue no live model calls.

[exclusion-01] Whether an obligation needs test evidence at all, which is #148.
    -> whether-obligation-needs-test-evidence-out-of-scope  [invariant/explicit]
       Whether an obligation needs test evidence at all is out of scope for this change.

[exclusion-02] Assigning obligation types, which is #205.
    -> assigning-obligation-types-out-of-scope  [invariant/explicit]
       Assigning obligation types is out of scope for this change.

[exclusion-03] Which open questions are raised, and what they cite, which is #206.
    -> open-questions-and-citations  [human_review/explicit]
       Raise open questions when the task text is materially underspecified, and include
       what each question cites.

[exclusion-04] How finely a single requirement is split into obligations, which is #117.
    -> requirement-splitting-granularity  [invariant/explicit]
       Preserve the specified granularity when splitting a single requirement into
       obligations.

[exclusion-05] Whether obligation identifiers are stable across task-file edits, which
    is #231.
    -> stable-obligation-identifiers  [compatibility/explicit]
       Keep obligation identifiers stable across task-file edits.

[exclusion-06] Measuring how accurate decomposition is, which is #211.
    -> decomposition-accuracy-measurement  [explanation_observability/explicit]
       Measure how accurate the decomposition is.

